WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.001 --> 00:00:04.839
[dramatic music playing]

2
00:01:03.230 --> 00:01:04.899
[explosion]

3
00:01:05.399 --> 00:01:07.359
[gunfire]

4
00:01:14.950 --> 00:01:18.746
[dramatic music playing]

5
00:01:39.975 --> 00:01:41.352
[explosion]

6
00:01:46.565 --> 00:01:49.819
[dramatic music continues]

7
00:02:10.464 --> 00:02:12.007
Goddamn it. Evans!

8
00:02:12.091 --> 00:02:13.133
Be careful.

9
00:02:13.217 --> 00:02:16.178
Sorry. Top. It's these damn roads.
It's fucking pea soup out there.

10
00:02:16.262 --> 00:02:21.308
Didn't you. um. tell me you was
a professional truck driver in Chicago?

11
00:02:21.392 --> 00:02:24.270
Detroit. First Sergeant. and yeah.

12
00:02:24.353 --> 00:02:26.397
Well. then. why don't you
quit your yapping

13
00:02:26.480 --> 00:02:28.041
and let's get these
resupplies to Schoenberg

14
00:02:28.065 --> 00:02:29.066
and we'd be done?

15
00:02:29.149 --> 00:02:30.401
Yeah. Top.

16
00:02:30.484 --> 00:02:32.403
Done would be real nice.

17
00:02:33.028 --> 00:02:35.072
Everybody's saying we
could be home by Christmas.

18
00:02:35.155 --> 00:02:37.116
What the fuck are you
talking about. Evans?

19
00:02:37.199 --> 00:02:39.010
These bastards just broke
through our front line

20
00:02:39.034 --> 00:02:40.578
like an ax through butter.

21
00:02:40.661 --> 00:02:43.455
and they planned in the worst weather
so we couldn't get air support.

22
00:02:44.248 --> 00:02:45.499
They ain't stupid.

23
00:02:46.458 --> 00:02:48.460
And it's dangerous thinking it's over.

24
00:02:48.544 --> 00:02:50.856
It ain't goddamn over.
and I don't know if it'll ever be over.

25
00:02:50.880 --> 00:02:52.006
Just keep driving. Evans.

26
00:02:52.089 --> 00:02:53.465
We gotta be there by 08:00.

27
00:02:54.341 --> 00:02:56.969
[ominous music playing]

28
00:03:09.565 --> 00:03:10.566
God!

29
00:03:11.400 --> 00:03:12.693
-[groans]
-Fuck!

30
00:03:15.529 --> 00:03:16.780
[engine whirring]

31
00:03:17.448 --> 00:03:19.199
We gotta get out of here.

32
00:03:19.283 --> 00:03:21.243
Let me check on it.

33
00:03:21.911 --> 00:03:23.996
[engine whirring]

34
00:03:29.001 --> 00:03:31.253
[engine whirring]

35
00:03:31.337 --> 00:03:33.005
Stop. stop. stop!

36
00:03:33.088 --> 00:03:34.798
Evans. it's not gonna work.

37
00:03:34.882 --> 00:03:36.634
-[distant explosion]
-[Evans] Fuck.

38
00:03:42.014 --> 00:03:43.015
We're stuck. guys.

39
00:03:43.098 --> 00:03:44.367
Lancaster. help me with this winch.

40
00:03:44.391 --> 00:03:45.660
[soldier] What's going on. First Sergeant?

41
00:03:45.684 --> 00:03:47.311
[Lancaster] On it. Top.

42
00:03:47.394 --> 00:03:50.064
[vehicle approaching]

43
00:03:50.147 --> 00:03:53.734
-[soldier] What's that. Sarge?
-Don't move.

44
00:04:06.497 --> 00:04:08.624
[engine whirring]

45
00:04:15.673 --> 00:04:18.467
[gunfire]

46
00:04:33.941 --> 00:04:35.609
[SS soldier in German] Be careful!

47
00:04:45.786 --> 00:04:47.788
[distant explosion]

48
00:04:49.206 --> 00:04:50.624
[guns cock]

49
00:04:51.917 --> 00:04:52.918
Fire!

50
00:04:57.798 --> 00:04:59.299
[US soldier groans]

51
00:04:59.967 --> 00:05:01.760
[gunshot]

52
00:05:03.387 --> 00:05:04.387
[in German] Go.

53
00:05:06.098 --> 00:05:07.808
Let's finish this.

54
00:05:07.891 --> 00:05:09.810
[gunfire]

55
00:05:09.893 --> 00:05:12.896
[in German] What was the name
of the Black American in Berlin?

56
00:05:13.397 --> 00:05:14.606
[SS soldier] Jesse Owens.

57
00:05:16.066 --> 00:05:20.279
They all look the same.
But they don't all run the same.

58
00:05:20.362 --> 00:05:22.322
[SS soldiers laugh]

59
00:05:22.865 --> 00:05:25.993
We're ten hours late. Let's go!

60
00:05:26.076 --> 00:05:28.746
[dramatic music playing]

61
00:05:36.295 --> 00:05:38.797
-Let's go.
-I hate Lucky Strikes.

62
00:05:38.881 --> 00:05:41.633
-Shut your mouth. Faster!
-Yes. sir.

63
00:05:47.973 --> 00:05:50.350
Let Schmidt lie there.
We don't have time for him.

64
00:05:51.810 --> 00:05:52.810
Yes. sir.

65
00:05:58.776 --> 00:06:00.319
I said get in!

66
00:06:02.780 --> 00:06:05.783
[engine whirring]

67
00:06:05.866 --> 00:06:08.702
[dramatic music playing]

68
00:06:21.340 --> 00:06:22.674
[knocking on door]

69
00:06:25.969 --> 00:06:27.554
[door lock clicking]

70
00:06:30.307 --> 00:06:31.747
[colonel. in English] Mrs. Caldwell?

71
00:06:32.851 --> 00:06:33.977
Yes.

72
00:06:34.853 --> 00:06:36.021
Hi.

73
00:06:36.105 --> 00:06:37.689
My name's John Castle.

74
00:06:37.773 --> 00:06:39.733
I'm a colonel in the United States Army.

75
00:06:39.817 --> 00:06:42.820
I got your name and address from Galvin.

76
00:06:46.031 --> 00:06:47.658
Yes. what can I do for you?

77
00:06:48.867 --> 00:06:51.912
Well. I'm here to talk about
your pension plan. ma'am.

78
00:06:53.580 --> 00:06:55.207
Do you work with Galvin?

79
00:06:55.874 --> 00:06:57.084
I... I do.

80
00:06:57.835 --> 00:07:00.879
But ma'am. I promise
this... this won't take long.

81
00:07:03.882 --> 00:07:05.259
99th Infantry.

82
00:07:05.342 --> 00:07:08.095
99th Division. 324th Engineers.

83
00:07:09.221 --> 00:07:10.222
Hmm.

84
00:07:11.682 --> 00:07:13.517
Battle of the Bulge.

85
00:07:14.434 --> 00:07:15.644
That's correct.

86
00:07:16.186 --> 00:07:17.771
Hmm.

87
00:07:17.855 --> 00:07:19.189
Yeah. my son.

88
00:07:20.190 --> 00:07:23.652
my son was there too. 761st.

89
00:07:24.486 --> 00:07:25.926
[Castle] It's quite a unit. I heard.

90
00:07:26.155 --> 00:07:27.072
They ah...

91
00:07:27.156 --> 00:07:30.325
Colonel Castle. you said
you worked for Galvin?

92
00:07:30.409 --> 00:07:32.161
With them. not for them.

93
00:07:32.244 --> 00:07:34.180
Well. my lawyer says that
I'm not supposed to be talking

94
00:07:34.204 --> 00:07:36.957
to anybody that works with Galvin.

95
00:07:41.503 --> 00:07:44.256
Is that coffee that I smell. ma'am?

96
00:07:47.384 --> 00:07:48.677
Yeah. I just...

97
00:07:48.760 --> 00:07:50.637
I just put on some. Would you like some?

98
00:07:50.721 --> 00:07:52.472
Like my life depends on it.

99
00:08:02.107 --> 00:08:03.609
I can't believe Galvin Industries

100
00:08:03.692 --> 00:08:06.028
has given away my whereabouts like that.

101
00:08:07.529 --> 00:08:08.530
Well.

102
00:08:09.573 --> 00:08:12.367
there was a lot of persuasion
and a little sweet talk.

103
00:08:13.827 --> 00:08:16.038
I assure you. it didn't come easy. ma'am.

104
00:08:17.164 --> 00:08:19.374
They're a very serious corporation.

105
00:08:20.792 --> 00:08:23.337
Very. very serious people over there.

106
00:08:23.420 --> 00:08:25.380
Oh. I know that for sure.

107
00:08:26.882 --> 00:08:28.675
They're very serious

108
00:08:30.594 --> 00:08:32.721
about not paying me my pension.

109
00:08:33.555 --> 00:08:35.015
Thank you.

110
00:08:38.101 --> 00:08:40.187
-That's why I'm here. ma'am.
-Is that right?

111
00:08:40.896 --> 00:08:41.897
Yes. ma'am.

112
00:08:41.980 --> 00:08:44.441
Well. I have been
threatening them for years.

113
00:08:46.235 --> 00:08:49.238
They know that I don't have the money
to take them to court.

114
00:08:50.489 --> 00:08:52.574
Are you some kind of army lawyer?

115
00:08:52.658 --> 00:08:53.909
No. no.

116
00:08:55.077 --> 00:08:57.287
But I know some of the folks
over at Galvin.

117
00:08:57.371 --> 00:08:59.790
and I do know that they
hold you in high regard.

118
00:08:59.873 --> 00:09:02.167
[scoffs] Me?

119
00:09:02.251 --> 00:09:03.835
-[Castle] Mm-hmm.
-Really?

120
00:09:04.419 --> 00:09:06.088
Top of the line employee.

121
00:09:06.171 --> 00:09:08.674
Yeah. that's what they said.
top of the line employee.

122
00:09:09.174 --> 00:09:11.009
Their words. right there in your file.

123
00:09:13.595 --> 00:09:15.806
Not that I need anyone to tell me. though.

124
00:09:17.057 --> 00:09:18.057
I know.

125
00:09:18.475 --> 00:09:19.476
You know?

126
00:09:19.559 --> 00:09:20.560
Hmm.

127
00:09:21.979 --> 00:09:22.979
Firsthand.

128
00:09:25.816 --> 00:09:27.192
You don't mind. do you?

129
00:09:28.068 --> 00:09:29.403
