[distant explosions]

801
00:53:58.569 --> 00:54:00.279
[distant explosions]

802
00:54:16.629 --> 00:54:17.922
[distant explosion]

803
00:54:38.025 --> 00:54:40.528
[distant explosions]

804
00:55:32.079 --> 00:55:34.123
[kettle whistles]

805
00:55:56.645 --> 00:55:57.855
What the hell?

806
00:56:05.446 --> 00:56:07.573
[footsteps approaching]

807
00:56:12.661 --> 00:56:14.288
[grunts]

808
00:56:15.831 --> 00:56:17.666
[Castle grunts]

809
00:56:18.375 --> 00:56:20.503
-[impact thuds]
-[kettle whistles]

810
00:56:30.471 --> 00:56:32.807
[SS soldier speaking German]

811
00:56:44.777 --> 00:56:46.612
[dramatic music playing]

812
00:56:48.697 --> 00:56:50.324
[SS soldier speaking German]

813
00:57:03.963 --> 00:57:05.881
[SS soldier speaking German]

814
00:57:11.178 --> 00:57:14.014
[dramatic music intensifies]

815
00:57:28.696 --> 00:57:30.906
[SS soldier speaking German]

816
00:57:50.342 --> 00:57:51.886
[speaking German]

817
00:58:03.606 --> 00:58:06.066
[speaking German]

818
00:58:14.366 --> 00:58:16.202
[speaking German]

819
00:58:27.087 --> 00:58:28.505
[door closes]

820
00:58:32.259 --> 00:58:34.178
[speaking German]

821
00:58:35.846 --> 00:58:37.514
[floor creaking]

822
00:58:40.684 --> 00:58:42.228
[fire roars]

823
00:58:42.311 --> 00:58:43.896
[SS soldier screams]

824
00:58:43.979 --> 00:58:45.981
[dramatic music playing]

825
00:58:56.408 --> 00:58:58.160
[SS soldier groaning]

826
00:59:04.208 --> 00:59:06.210
[dramatic music intensifies]

827
00:59:32.569 --> 00:59:33.569
[explosion]

828
00:59:43.038 --> 00:59:45.708
[distant explosions]

829
00:59:47.334 --> 00:59:49.461
[pensive music playing]

830
01:00:29.710 --> 01:00:30.961
[Castle] Any station...

831
01:00:31.045 --> 01:00:32.796
Any station on this net?

832
01:00:33.881 --> 01:00:35.799
This is Derrick 06.

833
01:00:36.759 --> 01:00:38.969
Any Dauntless. over?

834
01:00:40.304 --> 01:00:42.222
[radio operator] Dauntless.
how you holding up?

835
01:00:42.306 --> 01:00:45.726
[Castle] Dauntless. I...
I steered clear of Bellingen.

836
01:00:46.518 --> 01:00:48.687
I think I'm back on track.

837
01:00:48.771 --> 01:00:52.441
traveling north
by northwest to rally point.

838
01:00:52.524 --> 01:00:54.169
[radio operator]
They're surrounding our southern side.

839
01:00:54.193 --> 01:00:56.236
which means you're behind enemy lines.

840
01:00:56.320 --> 01:00:57.446
They're pounding us.

841
01:00:57.529 --> 01:00:58.989
Find shelter.

842
01:00:59.073 --> 01:01:00.866
[Castle] No. negative. Dauntless.

843
01:01:00.949 --> 01:01:02.826
There is no shelter.

844
01:01:02.910 --> 01:01:04.495
I need to keep moving.

845
01:01:04.578 --> 01:01:05.764
I'll take my chances to get to you.

846
01:01:05.788 --> 01:01:07.098
[radio operator] Just be careful.

847
01:01:07.122 --> 01:01:09.166
1st SS is gonna unload
everything they have.

848
01:01:09.249 --> 01:01:10.376
Good luck.

849
01:01:11.835 --> 01:01:13.170
[groans]

850
01:01:19.009 --> 01:01:20.260
[groans]

851
01:01:21.678 --> 01:01:22.846
Oh. my God.

852
01:01:23.972 --> 01:01:24.972
Oh.

853
01:01:26.058 --> 01:01:27.142
Jesus.

854
01:01:33.565 --> 01:01:35.651
[soldier coughs]

855
01:01:35.734 --> 01:01:37.694
Oh. hey.

856
01:01:38.737 --> 01:01:39.738
Hey.

857
01:01:40.656 --> 01:01:41.657
Hey.

858
01:01:42.199 --> 01:01:43.700
Hey. hey.

859
01:01:43.784 --> 01:01:45.035
Are you okay?

860
01:01:46.245 --> 01:01:47.704
Oh. man.

861
01:01:47.788 --> 01:01:50.040
Other than being shot twice.

862
01:01:50.124 --> 01:01:51.125
All right. Sergeant.

863
01:01:52.167 --> 01:01:53.168
Yeah.

864
01:01:55.129 --> 01:01:58.006
Hey. what's your name. huh?

865
01:01:58.090 --> 01:01:59.007
Maren.

866
01:01:59.091 --> 01:02:01.135
Maren. that's your first name?

867
01:02:01.218 --> 01:02:03.262
-[explosion]
-Pierce.

868
01:02:03.345 --> 01:02:04.555
Pierce.

869
01:02:04.638 --> 01:02:05.556
Pierce.

870
01:02:05.639 --> 01:02:07.433
The truck work?

871
01:02:07.516 --> 01:02:10.602
-Yeah. but it's stuck.
-It's stuck.

872
01:02:10.686 --> 01:02:11.812
-[Pierce coughs]
-Okay.

873
01:02:11.895 --> 01:02:13.397
Okay. okay.

874
01:02:13.480 --> 01:02:15.399
Look. I'm gonna...

875
01:02:17.234 --> 01:02:20.028
I'm gonna get this thing unstuck. okay?

876
01:02:20.112 --> 01:02:22.072
-Any water?
-Water?

877
01:02:22.156 --> 01:02:23.073
Oh. yeah.

878
01:02:23.157 --> 01:02:24.450
Yeah. sorry.

879
01:02:24.533 --> 01:02:25.951
Yeah. of course.

880
01:02:28.328 --> 01:02:29.413
Here.

881
01:02:29.496 --> 01:02:31.248
Come on. come on.

882
01:02:31.331 --> 01:02:32.583
Come on. here.

883
01:02:32.666 --> 01:02:34.668
Come on. come on.

884
01:02:34.751 --> 01:02:36.503
Yeah. there you go.

885
01:02:36.587 --> 01:02:37.588
Oh. shit.

886
01:02:40.174 --> 01:02:41.800
Okay.

887
01:02:41.884 --> 01:02:45.179
Oh. man. I need a rope
or something to get this out of here.

888
01:02:45.262 --> 01:02:46.263
Shit.

889
01:02:48.515 --> 01:02:50.642
-You gotta use the winch.
-Winch.

890
01:02:50.726 --> 01:02:52.227
Oh. there's a winch. good.

891
01:02:52.311 --> 01:02:53.687
Okay. good call.

892
01:02:54.354 --> 01:02:56.231
[grunts. groans]

893
01:02:56.315 --> 01:02:58.817
Okay. I'm gonna get this thing.

894
01:03:01.195 --> 01:03:03.030
[Pierce coughs]

895
01:03:09.995 --> 01:03:11.371
[Castle blowing]

896
01:03:13.790 --> 01:03:17.169
Come on. man. you need
to talk to me. okay?

897
01:03:17.252 --> 01:03:20.339
Pierce. you talk to me. okay?

898
01:03:21.256 --> 01:03:22.257
Fuck.

899
01:03:24.343 --> 01:03:25.677
So. where are you from?

900
01:03:25.761 --> 01:03:27.137
[Pierce] Bridgeport.

901
01:03:27.221 --> 01:03:29.389
Ah. Connecticut. [groans]

902
01:03:30.098 --> 01:03:31.600
[grunts] Never been.

903
01:03:32.935 --> 01:03:33.936
I hear it's...

904
01:03:34.019 --> 01:03:35.020
I hear it's nice there.

905
01:03:35.103 --> 01:03:36.271
Is that true?

906
01:03:36.355 --> 01:03:38.273
[Pierce] Yeah. I think you'd like it.

907
01:03:38.357 --> 01:03:39.816
Pierce. Pierce.

908
01:03:39.900 --> 01:03:41.360
-[Pierce coughs]
-Come on.

909
01:03:41.443 --> 01:03:43.153
Come on. pal. stay with me.

910
01:03:44.905 --> 01:03:46.532
How long you been out here. huh?

911
01:03:49.952 --> 01:03:50.952
Long time.

912
01:03:50.994 --> 01:03:52.329
All right. long time.

913
01:03:52.412 --> 01:03:54.164
All right. all right.

914
01:03:54.248 --> 01:03:55.832
Tell me. are you ready to go home?

915
01:03:55.916 --> 01:03:56.916
[explosion]

916
01:03:57.876 --> 01:03:58.961
[explosion]

917
01:04:07.886 --> 01:04:10.430
[high-pitched ringing]

918
01:04:16.562 --> 01:04:18.272
-[object clicks]
-[groans]

919
01:04:19.940 --> 01:04:21.233
[explosion]

920
01:04:59.855 --> 01:05:02.524
[foreboding music playing]

921
01:05:28.467 --> 01:05:30.927
[music fades]

922
01:05:42.397 --> 01:05:43.940
[horse chuffs]

923
01:05:56.370 --> 01:05:57.746
-[Castle screams]
-[horse whinnies]

924
01:05:57.829 --> 01:05:58.829
Shit!

925
01:06:01.083 --> 01:06:02.626
[horse whinnies]

926
01:06:14.179 --> 01:06:16.807
[gunfire]

927
01:06:22.187 --> 01:06:23.187
Shit!

928
01:06:26.900 --> 01:06:28.860
[Castle screams]

929
01:06:31.488 --> 01:06:34.074
-[gunfire]
-[explosions]

930
01:06:49.798 --> 01:06:50.882
Stop. please.

931
01:06:50.966 --> 01:06:51.967
Stop.

932
01:06:54.177 --> 01:06:55.220
Please. God.

933
01:06:59.850 --> 01:07:01.226
[Castle screams]

934
01:07:01.852 --> 01:07:04.396
Help. please. Take me home.

935
01:07:09.818 --> 01:07:10.694
Hunter.

936
01:07:10.777 --> 01:07:12.154
[inaudible]

937
01:07:21.413 --> 01:07:23.623
[Castle coughs]

938
01:07:38.680 --> 01:07:40.056
[groans]

939
01:07:54.613 --> 01:07:55.989
[chain rattling]

940
01:07:58.325 --> 01:07:59.951
[chain rattling]

941
01:08:10.837 --> 01:08:12.005
[dog barking]

942
01:08:14.424 --> 01:08:16.802
[soldier] Hey. stop! Fido. quiet. hey!

943
01:08:16.885 --> 01:08:18.303
Quiet. hey. American.

944
01:08:18.386 --> 01:08:19.596
Who are you?

945
01:08:23.600 --> 01:08:25.977
Captain Castle. 324th engineers.

946
01:08:26.061 --> 01:08:27.246
Sergeant Bellingham. sir. 14th...

947
01:08:27.270 --> 01:08:29.397
-[Castle] Agh!
-Ooh. ooh.

948
01:08:30.065 --> 01:08:31.817
I got you. I got you.

949
01:08:36.988 --> 01:08:38.424
Here. let me help you with your radio.

950
01:08:38.448 --> 01:08:39.908
[Castle] Ah. yeah. yeah.

951
01:08:44.663 --> 01:08:45.956
You okay?

952
01:08:46.039 --> 01:08:48.041
-Looks like you took some shrapnel.
-Yeah.

953
01:08:51.253 --> 01:08:53.380
[Castle] Geez. what happened here?

954
01:08:53.463 --> 01:08:54.798
[Bellingham] Our willy's...

955
01:08:54.881 --> 01:08:56.299
Willy's got mortared. I think.

956
01:08:56.883 --> 01:08:58.677
I don't really remember what happened.

957
01:08:59.886 --> 01:09:01.179
What was that hell show anyway?

958
01:09:01.263 --> 01:09:02.597
Oh. I don't know.

959
01:09:03.557 --> 01:09:04.557
Yeah.

960
01:09:08.979 --> 01:09:10.248
[Bellingham] That looks
pretty severe. sir.

961
01:09:10.272 --> 01:09:12.649
We should... we should
get you sitting down.

962
01:09:14.609 --> 01:09:16.027
I got you. sir.

963
01:09:18.113 --> 01:09:19.614
-[Castle groans]
-There you go.

964
01:09:30.041 --> 01:09:31.042
So.

965
01:09:32.168 --> 01:09:33.587
where were you headed before this?

966
01:09:34.671 --> 01:09:38.633
I need to get to the 99th Division command

967
01:09:38.717 --> 01:09:40.677
and get a package to the commander.

968
01:09:41.887 --> 01:09:42.888
General Lauer?

969
01:09:44.055 --> 01:09:45.390
-Yes. sir.
-Yeah.

970
01:09:46.975 --> 01:09:47.851
Okay.

971
01:09:47.934 --> 01:09:50.437
I don't know their position now. do you?

972
01:09:50.520 --> 01:09:52.230
No. I don't.

973
01:09:52.314 --> 01:09:54.774
I'm only in contact
with battalion. not division.

974
01:09:55.984 --> 01:09:58.653
You have a priority frequency for him?

975
01:09:58.737 --> 01:10:01.781
If you do. we could... we could try him.

976
01:10:01.865 --> 01:10:03.617
It's above my pay grade.

977
01:10:03.700 --> 01:10:04.700
Right.

978
01:10:04.743 --> 01:10:06.536
We'll try the 324th then.

979
01:10:06.620 --> 01:10:07.621
That'd be great.

980
01:10:07.704 --> 01:10:09.539
I have to courier these reports on them.

981
01:10:09.623 --> 01:10:11.374
Yeah. Yeah. you said that.

982
01:10:11.458 --> 01:10:12.918
Progress of the Third Army.

983
01:10:13.001 --> 01:10:15.378
What. Patton's not allowing

984
01:10:15.462 --> 01:10:16.922
scrambled lines between armies now?

985
01:10:21.009 --> 01:10:23.178
I can't see anything.

986
01:10:23.261 --> 01:10:25.472
Can you turn that on... on for me?

987
01:10:25.555 --> 01:10:27.432
[Bellingham] Let's see if it even works.

988
01:10:30.101 --> 01:10:31.394
Patton. huh?

989
01:10:31.478 --> 01:10:33.021
Great general.

990
01:10:33.104 --> 01:10:34.648
Huge pain in the ass.

991
01:10:34.731 --> 01:10:35.649
[Bellingham] Yes.

992
01:10:35.732 --> 01:10:36.733
Thanks.

993
01:10:37.609 --> 01:10:39.027
What about you. sir?

994
01:10:39.110 --> 01:10:40.630
What are you doing out here? You uh...

995
01:10:40.654 --> 01:10:42.854
you get separated from your unit
or something like that?

996
01:10:44.074 --> 01:10:45.700
-Yeah.
-[dog panting]

997
01:10:45.784 --> 01:10:47.953
Yeah. something like that.

998
01:10:49.287 --> 01:10:50.330
Are you hungry. sir?

999
01:10:50.413 --> 01:10:51.623
It's tuna loaf.

1000
01:10:51.706 --> 01:10:52.791
[Castle] Oh. thanks.

1001
01:10:54.125 --> 01:10:55.460
[Bellingham mutters to dog]

1002
01:10:55.543 --> 01:10:57.420
Oh. good boy.

1003
01:10:57.504 --> 01:10:58.630
Good boy.

1004
01:11:01.424 --> 01:11:02.425
Nice trophy.

1005
01:11:02.509 --> 01:11:03.593
Huh?

1006
01:11:05.178 --> 01:11:06.429
You got a Luger.

1007
01:11:06.513 --> 01:11:08.240
I've been trying to find one
of those since I got here.

1008
01:11:08.264 --> 01:11:10.350
[Castle] Oh. yeah. yeah.

1009
01:11:13.061 --> 01:11:14.688
I just gotta find that station.

1010
01:11:16.564 --> 01:11:19.734
[Castle] Oh. come on. old girl.
Come on. please.

1011
01:11:24.698 --> 01:11:25.699
I got nothing.

1012
01:11:26.366 --> 01:11:28.206
[Bellingham] I think
the battery's still alive.

1013
01:11:29.119 --> 01:11:30.286
Do you mind. sir?

1014
01:11:31.830 --> 01:11:33.873
Yeah. she's pretty beat up.

1015
01:11:33.957 --> 01:11:36.668
You a... you a radio guy?

1016
01:11:36.751 --> 01:11:37.961
Let me see.

1017
01:11:43.049 --> 01:11:44.092
Lassie. huh?

1018
01:11:45.343 --> 01:11:46.845
Yeah. yeah. man.

1019
01:11:46.928 --> 01:11:49.014
Our radio operator named her that.

1020
01:11:50.765 --> 01:11:53.435
Seemed fitting how reliable
she's been till now.

1021
01:11:54.602 --> 01:11:58.064
Yeah. I'm more of
a Rin Tin Tin man myself.

1022
01:11:58.148 --> 01:11:59.399
[radio hisses static]

1023
01:11:59.482 --> 01:12:02.652
[chuckles] She may be reliable after all.

1024
01:12:02.736 --> 01:12:04.446
-How about that?
-Yeah.

1025
01:12:04.529 --> 01:12:06.823
-Oh. good work. knew it.
-She's receiving.

1026
01:12:08.033 --> 01:12:09.868
-Good work.
-Yeah.

1027
01:12:09.951 --> 01:12:11.578
Okay.

1028
01:12:11.661 --> 01:12:13.788
Oh. shit. sir. You're bleeding out.

1029
01:12:13.872 --> 01:12:15.623
[Castle] Yeah. I know.

1030
01:12:15.707 --> 01:12:17.792
-That's not good.
-Mm-mm.

1031
01:12:17.876 --> 01:12:21.254
[Castle] Let's just focus on
getting out... out of here.

1032
01:12:21.921 --> 01:12:26.342
Yeah. you have a point guy at the 99th?

1033
01:12:26.426 --> 01:12:27.426
No. no. no. no.

1034
01:12:27.469 --> 01:12:30.555
I was supposed to report to HQ directly.

1035
01:12:30.638 --> 01:12:34.017
[sniffs] I have the sealed positions
maps with me. but I don't...

1036
01:12:34.559 --> 01:12:35.935
I don't know shit besides that.

1037
01:12:36.019 --> 01:12:37.854
All right. Any station?

1038
01:12:38.354 --> 01:12:39.856
Any station on this net?

1039
01:12:40.356 --> 01:12:41.357
Any station?

1040
01:12:41.858 --> 01:12:44.360
This is Derrick 06. over.

1041
01:12:44.444 --> 01:12:47.405
[radio hissing. tuning]

1042
01:12:48.448 --> 01:12:49.657
Yeah.

1043
01:12:49.741 --> 01:12:52.035
Nobody's home.

1044
01:12:52.118 --> 01:12:54.287
[distant explosion]

1045
01:12:54.370 --> 01:12:55.371
Krauts.

1046
01:12:56.831 --> 01:12:59.918
-They love to fight at night.
-Yeah. they can't...

1047
01:13:01.086 --> 01:13:02.545
They can't wait to.

1048
01:13:03.379 --> 01:13:05.423
to die for their fatherland.

1049
01:13:05.965 --> 01:13:06.966
[Bellingham] That's true.

1050
01:13:13.932 --> 01:13:15.058
I'll tell you why.

1051
01:13:15.642 --> 01:13:16.976
[Castle coughs]

1052
01:13:17.060 --> 01:13:19.479
Because they don't have much to live for.

1053
01:13:23.858 --> 01:13:25.110
Yeah. sorry.

1054
01:13:26.194 --> 01:13:28.071
Yeah. thank you. sir.

1055
01:13:36.454 --> 01:13:38.498
[Bellingham breathing deeply]

1056
01:13:42.168 --> 01:13:44.063
Like. when you say they
don't have much to live for.

1057
01:13:44.087 --> 01:13:46.881
I mean. from their point
of view. I don't know.

1058
01:13:46.965 --> 01:13:49.926
Hitler's given them a hell of an economy.

1059
01:13:51.010 --> 01:13:52.554
He gave them the Olympics.

1060
01:13:54.764 --> 01:13:56.808
And if I'm being honest.
every country has its...

1061
01:13:58.309 --> 01:13:59.644
undesirables.

1062
01:14:01.729 --> 01:14:03.409
I mean. look at what we did
to the Indians.

1063
01:14:04.566 --> 01:14:07.652
Look. don't get me wrong. okay?
Hitler's a... a monster.

1064
01:14:08.153 --> 01:14:09.154
He's a vile beast.

1065
01:14:09.237 --> 01:14:12.197
But when we don't understand them
and we don't understand what drives them.

1066
01:14:12.240 --> 01:14:13.867
then we underestimate them too.

1067
01:14:14.576 --> 01:14:15.618
Mm-hmm.

1068
01:14:16.744 --> 01:14:18.746
[radio operator] Derrick 06. Derrick 06.

1069
01:14:18.830 --> 01:14:20.623
do you copy. over?

1070
01:14:20.707 --> 01:14:24.460
Copy. copy. copy.
This is Derrick 06 actual.

1071
01:14:25.336 --> 01:14:27.231
[radio operator] Derrick.
we've secured Elsenborn.

1072
01:14:27.255 --> 01:14:29.215
We're trying to release
some assets to get to you.

1073
01:14:29.299 --> 01:14:32.051
Any idea where you are at all. over?

1074
01:14:32.135 --> 01:14:34.554
Ah. yeah. hold on. hold on.

1075
01:14:36.055 --> 01:14:37.182
[Castle] Okay.

1076
01:14:39.517 --> 01:14:42.729
Now. listen. I think
we're on the south side of...

1077
01:14:43.855 --> 01:14:45.857
Hittenberg maybe.

1078
01:14:45.940 --> 01:14:47.734
[radio operator] Roger. Did you say we?

1079
01:14:47.817 --> 01:14:49.777
Are you with somebody. over?

1080
01:14:49.861 --> 01:14:52.197
Yeah... yeah. I got a...

1081
01:14:52.780 --> 01:14:53.823
What is it. what is it?

1082
01:14:53.907 --> 01:14:54.908
Bellingham. Belling...

1083
01:14:54.991 --> 01:14:57.452
I got a Sergeant Bellingham here

1084
01:14:57.535 --> 01:15:01.456
who's assigned to deliver
maps to the 99th HQ.

1085
01:15:02.707 --> 01:15:04.709
You got a position for him?

1086
01:15:04.792 --> 01:15:06.878
[radio operator]
Okay. let me check on that. over.

1087
01:15:06.961 --> 01:15:09.130
[Castle] Copy. this way. Copy.

1088
01:15:13.593 --> 01:15:16.262
So. where are you from. huh?

1089
01:15:16.346 --> 01:15:17.430
Milwaukee.

1090
01:15:19.098 --> 01:15:22.435
Does that make you a Cubs
or a White Sox guy?

1091
01:15:22.518 --> 01:15:25.063
No. no. no. I'm not a...
not a big baseball guy.

1092
01:15:26.189 --> 01:15:27.482
So football then?

1093
01:15:27.565 --> 01:15:29.150
-Definitely. yeah.
-Yeah.

1094
01:15:29.234 --> 01:15:30.944
Yeah. that's my game.

1095
01:15:31.027 --> 01:15:32.707
Naval-Army game is like a national holiday

1096
01:15:32.779 --> 01:15:34.030
in my household.

1097
01:15:36.449 --> 01:15:39.369
[Bellingham] We gather around the radio
and listen to the game every year.

1098
01:15:39.619 --> 01:15:41.037
How long you been in?

1099
01:15:41.120 --> 01:15:42.872
God. I lost track of that.

1100
01:15:44.332 --> 01:15:47.627
They had me down in Africa driving tanks

1101
01:15:48.753 --> 01:15:50.838
until someone spilled the beans

1102
01:15:50.922 --> 01:15:54.676
and told 'em I was a engineer back home.

1103
01:15:56.427 --> 01:15:59.597
Now I'm up here blowing up bridges.

1104
01:16:01.975 --> 01:16:03.351
You got a girl back home?

1105
01:16:03.434 --> 01:16:05.353
[laughs] No.

1106
01:16:05.436 --> 01:16:08.022
No. I got my "Dear John"
two weeks into basic.

1107
01:16:09.148 --> 01:16:10.149
Yeah.

1108
01:16:10.858 --> 01:16:12.026
How about you?

1109
01:16:30.712 --> 01:16:32.839
[chuckles] Kids?

1110
01:16:33.631 --> 01:16:34.507
Yeah.

1111
01:16:34.590 --> 01:16:37.552
Yeah. one. my son. Hunter.

1112
01:16:39.470 --> 01:16:41.556
Looks like you'll be seeing him soon.

1113
01:16:41.639 --> 01:16:44.142
Yeah. that's the plan.

1114
01:16:46.769 --> 01:16:50.773
My wife lost her brother at Midway.
so I better get home.

1115
01:16:51.607 --> 01:16:52.775
Oh. you will. sir.

1116
01:16:53.860 --> 01:16:55.445
We're gonna get you back.

1117
01:16:58.031 --> 01:16:59.324
I'm gonna...

1118
01:16:59.407 --> 01:17:00.950
I'm gonna take care of business.

1119
01:17:01.034 --> 01:17:02.118
I'll be back.

1120
01:17:03.619 --> 01:17:05.121
[coughs]

1121
01:17:08.333 --> 01:17:10.418
[Fido yawns]

1122
01:17:14.088 --> 01:17:16.174
[distant explosions]

1123
01:17:31.814 --> 01:17:34.692
[pensive music playing]

1124
01:17:49.540 --> 01:17:52.335
[ominous music playing]

1125
01:18:04.055 --> 01:18:05.139
Uh...

1126
01:18:06.099 --> 01:18:11.270
Uh. who'd you say you take
again in the Naval-Army?

1127
01:18:12.480 --> 01:18:13.523
[Bellingham] What?

1128
01:18:14.649 --> 01:18:16.818
[radio operator] Derrick 06. do you copy?

1129
01:18:21.322 --> 01:18:22.198
Yeah.

1130
01:18:22.281 --> 01:18:24.075
Yeah. copy. copy.

1131
01:18:24.158 --> 01:18:26.119
[radio operator]
Okay. prepare to write down.

1132
01:18:30.623 --> 01:18:31.749
Yeah. go ahead.

1133
01:18:31.833 --> 01:18:36.337
[radio operator] SOI.
Baker. Charlie. X-ray.

1134
01:18:37.130 --> 01:18:38.339
yoke.

1135
01:18:38.423 --> 01:18:39.882
love.

1136
01:18:39.966 --> 01:18:41.092
able.

1137
01:18:41.175 --> 01:18:42.343
tare.

1138
01:18:42.427 --> 01:18:43.761
uncle.

1139
01:18:45.596 --> 01:18:46.597
Over.

1140
01:18:46.681 --> 01:18:47.681
[Castle] Yeah.

1141
01:18:49.142 --> 01:18:50.226
Copy.

1142
01:18:50.309 --> 01:18:52.395
[ominous music continues]

1143
01:18:53.980 --> 01:18:56.732
[Castle] Hey. do me a favor.

1144
01:18:56.816 --> 01:18:58.234
Tell the guys.

1145
01:18:58.317 --> 01:19:00.319
tell the guys to step on it. okay?

1146
01:19:01.696 --> 01:19:02.613
I'm in bad shape.

1147
01:19:02.697 --> 01:19:04.550
[radio operator] Godspeed
to you. Captain Castle.

1148
01:19:04.574 --> 01:19:05.908
Out.

1149
01:19:05.992 --> 01:19:07.326
Godspeed.

1150
01:19:14.876 --> 01:19:17.086
[Castle] Here. here's the info.

1151
01:19:18.004 --> 01:19:20.298
-That's the position of HQ.
-Thank you. sir.

1152
01:19:26.888 --> 01:19:28.764
[chuckles]

1153
01:19:32.226 --> 01:19:34.026
You don't know
what you're looking at. do you?

1154
01:19:34.103 --> 01:19:38.524
Like I said. it's...
it's above my pay grade.

1155
01:19:43.696 --> 01:19:45.531
It's an SOI encoding.

1156
01:19:47.533 --> 01:19:51.913
SOI. signal operating instructions.

1157
01:19:53.831 --> 01:19:54.999
But you wouldn't know that.

1158
01:19:55.708 --> 01:19:56.708
Sir.

1159
01:19:57.835 --> 01:19:59.420
please put the weapon down.

1160
01:19:59.504 --> 01:20:01.672
You mean my... my trophy?

1161
01:20:01.756 --> 01:20:02.924
Sir.

1162
01:20:03.591 --> 01:20:06.719
you've been badly injured. okay?

1163
01:20:06.802 --> 01:20:08.362
-You're not thinking straight.
-Shut up!

1164
01:20:09.805 --> 01:20:11.682
No one... no one taught you

1165
01:20:11.766 --> 01:20:14.060
how to light up a Lucky
the right way. did they?

1166
01:20:14.143 --> 01:20:15.853
-Please. sir.
-You see. we do this

1167
01:20:15.937 --> 01:20:18.064
so we don't leave
breadcrumbs for you assholes.

1168
01:20:18.147 --> 01:20:18.981
Please. sir.

1169
01:20:19.065 --> 01:20:21.108
Next time. think of that. fucker.

1170
01:20:22.527 --> 01:20:25.863
They warned us about scumbags like you.

1171
01:20:25.947 --> 01:20:29.075
born in America yet killing Americans.

1172
01:20:30.660 --> 01:20:32.912
You think because I smoke
a cigarette a different way

1173
01:20:32.995 --> 01:20:34.539
that I'm a Nazi sympathizer?

1174
01:20:34.622 --> 01:20:37.500
Not a sympathizer. a Nazi!

1175
01:20:37.583 --> 01:20:39.544
I told you I'm not SS.
I'm a fucking American.

1176
01:20:39.627 --> 01:20:41.420
Oh. yeah. really?

1177
01:20:41.504 --> 01:20:42.672
-Yes. sir. I'm...
-Show me.

1178
01:20:42.755 --> 01:20:46.467
Show me you don't have a SS tattoo
underneath your arm.

1179
01:20:47.552 --> 01:20:50.555
[radio operator]
Derrick 06. Derrick. copy. over?

1180
01:20:50.638 --> 01:20:52.056
-[Fido barking]
-[gunshot]

1181
01:20:57.812 --> 01:20:59.188
[gunfire]

1182
01:20:59.272 --> 01:21:01.566
[Castle groans]

1183
01:21:05.486 --> 01:21:07.697
[Fido barking]

1184
01:21:14.495 --> 01:21:16.038
[coughs]

1185
01:21:19.542 --> 01:21:20.793
Two left.

1186
01:21:30.303 --> 01:21:31.304
[gunfire]

1187
01:21:33.097 --> 01:21:34.890
[Fido barking]

1188
01:21:42.398 --> 01:21:44.483
-[gunfire]
-[Fido whimpers]

1189
01:21:47.069 --> 01:21:48.654
[gunfire]

1190
01:21:51.449 --> 01:21:53.200
[suspenseful music playing]

1191
01:21:55.745 --> 01:21:56.996
[gunshot]

1192
01:21:59.373 --> 01:22:00.916
[gunfire]

1193
01:22:06.005 --> 01:22:08.090
-[gunshot]
-[Bellingham groans]

1194
01:22:13.596 --> 01:22:14.805
[groaning]

1195
01:22:25.983 --> 01:22:27.193
[Castle grunts]

1196
01:22:42.333 --> 01:22:45.336
[radio operator] Derrick 06.
this is Dublin 06 Rider.

1197
01:22:45.419 --> 01:22:46.671
Over.

1198
01:22:46.754 --> 01:22:49.131
-Derrick 06. Derrick 06. do you copy?
-[radio crackles]

1199
01:22:49.965 --> 01:22:51.133
Over.

1200
01:22:51.217 --> 01:22:55.096
[on radio] ♪ I'll be home ♪

1201
01:22:55.179 --> 01:23:00.309
♪ For Christmas ♪

1202
01:23:00.393 --> 01:23:06.982
♪ If only in my dreams ♪

1203
01:23:10.027 --> 01:23:12.655
[engine whirring]

1204
01:23:23.666 --> 01:23:26.127
[Castle] Where's Lassie?

1205
01:23:26.210 --> 01:23:28.003
Are you okay. sir? Can you hear me?

1206
01:23:28.087 --> 01:23:30.214
[Castle] Where. where. where...
Where are we?

1207
01:23:30.297 --> 01:23:32.442
You're doing great. sir.
We're almost at the field hospital.

1208
01:23:32.466 --> 01:23:33.759
[Castle] Where's the radio?

1209
01:23:33.843 --> 01:23:35.428
Right here. sir.

1210
01:23:59.034 --> 01:24:00.661
[nurse] I'll be back shortly.

1211
01:24:03.164 --> 01:24:04.373
Captain Castle?

1212
01:24:04.457 --> 01:24:06.083
Yes. sir. he's right over there.

1213
01:24:06.792 --> 01:24:09.336
-Good afternoon. Captain.
-[Castle groans]

1214
01:24:09.420 --> 01:24:10.647
Good to have you still with us.

1215
01:24:10.671 --> 01:24:12.089
Sir.

1216
01:24:12.173 --> 01:24:13.215
At ease. son.

1217
01:24:13.299 --> 01:24:14.884
Relax.

1218
01:24:14.967 --> 01:24:16.177
I'm General Lauer.

1219
01:24:16.260 --> 01:24:17.261
Nice to meet you. sir.

1220
01:24:18.721 --> 01:24:21.807
From what we've been able to ascertain.

1221
01:24:21.891 --> 01:24:23.476
you've really been through it.

1222
01:24:24.477 --> 01:24:26.812
[Lauer] Left a lot of dead Nazis
in your wake.

1223
01:24:27.897 --> 01:24:31.025
And that abatis you created
stopped them in their tracks

1224
01:24:31.901 --> 01:24:33.694
and bought us some precious hours.

1225
01:24:35.571 --> 01:24:36.405
[Castle] Yeah.

1226
01:24:36.489 --> 01:24:38.169
But that final position you ended up in...

1227
01:24:38.240 --> 01:24:39.492
I don't even...

1228
01:24:40.618 --> 01:24:44.830
remember or know what happened. really.

1229
01:24:45.915 --> 01:24:49.835
Those goddamn Krauts blew
the hell out of that place

1230
01:24:49.919 --> 01:24:51.796
because they were trying to create

1231
01:24:51.879 --> 01:24:54.423
a path for themselves to Elsenborn.

1232
01:24:55.382 --> 01:24:57.009
It's just your bad luck you were there.

1233
01:24:59.553 --> 01:25:00.781
I want you to know we're putting you in

1234
01:25:00.805 --> 01:25:02.890
for the Silver Star captain.

1235
01:25:02.973 --> 01:25:04.391
You damn well deserve it.

1236
01:25:05.226 --> 01:25:06.393
Oh. I...

1237
01:25:07.937 --> 01:25:09.772
What about the. uh.

1238
01:25:09.855 --> 01:25:13.234
the soldier. the guy where you found me?

1239
01:25:13.317 --> 01:25:16.779
Yes. he was SS posing as an American.

1240
01:25:16.862 --> 01:25:19.406
He's dead. You got him.

1241
01:25:20.866 --> 01:25:22.243
And our intel tells us

1242
01:25:22.326 --> 01:25:24.638
that they were trying to find
the location of General Lauer.

1243
01:25:24.662 --> 01:25:28.249
so you were right in shooting the bastard.

1244
01:25:28.332 --> 01:25:29.708
Right.

1245
01:25:29.792 --> 01:25:31.210
How did you know. by the way?

1246
01:25:33.003 --> 01:25:34.129
Oh. he. uh...

1247
01:25:35.130 --> 01:25:36.674
he said some wrong things.

1248
01:25:37.842 --> 01:25:41.470
And he didn't burn
the brand off his Luckies.

1249
01:25:44.056 --> 01:25:45.474
Sin number one.

1250
01:25:46.517 --> 01:25:49.562
Well. three cheers
for shitty German training.

1251
01:25:51.355 --> 01:25:53.232
You look like you could
use a bit more rest.

1252
01:25:53.315 --> 01:25:55.025
so see you soon.

1253
01:25:55.109 --> 01:25:57.278
Sir. I... I don't...

1254
01:25:59.280 --> 01:26:00.656
All my men are dead.

1255
01:26:02.283 --> 01:26:04.451
Yes. I know.

1256
01:26:04.535 --> 01:26:06.287
and I'm very sorry.

1257
01:26:06.370 --> 01:26:10.291
Yeah. I just don't think
that I deserve any kind of medal.

1258
01:26:11.000 --> 01:26:12.960
Luckily. that's not for you to decide.

1259
01:26:13.043 --> 01:26:15.421
Well. with all due respect. sir.

1260
01:26:15.504 --> 01:26:19.049
I just gotta say no. thank you.

1261
01:26:20.718 --> 01:26:23.804
I'm an officer
and keeping my men safe. that...

1262
01:26:24.305 --> 01:26:26.015
that's my job. and I failed that.

1263
01:26:26.098 --> 01:26:27.683
That's really what you think.

1264
01:26:28.434 --> 01:26:30.311
that your job is to keep your men alive?

1265
01:26:30.895 --> 01:26:32.146
Yes. sir.

1266
01:26:34.189 --> 01:26:35.441
Well. that's. uh...

1267
01:26:36.942 --> 01:26:38.485
That's a crock of shit. son.

1268
01:26:42.406 --> 01:26:43.782
Soldiers die in war.

1269
01:26:45.326 --> 01:26:47.828
Your job is not to keep your men alive.

1270
01:26:48.871 --> 01:26:51.081
Your job is to keep my mother alive.

1271
01:26:52.124 --> 01:26:54.043
Your job is to keep your mother alive.

1272
01:26:54.126 --> 01:26:56.629
Your job is to keep
all our children alive.

1273
01:26:58.505 --> 01:26:59.590
So...

1274
01:27:00.382 --> 01:27:03.677
with all due respect. Captain.
you can take your no thanks

1275
01:27:03.761 --> 01:27:06.513
and you can shove it up your ass.

1276
01:27:12.686 --> 01:27:14.229
A bit of a miracle. those things. huh?

1277
01:27:14.980 --> 01:27:17.566
Hmm. bit more reliable than a miracle.

1278
01:27:21.403 --> 01:27:22.488
Get some rest.

1279
01:27:38.921 --> 01:27:40.214
[sighs]

1280
01:28:16.291 --> 01:28:18.460
[soldier] Get the deuce and a half ready!

1281
01:28:21.797 --> 01:28:22.797
[Cash] Hey. sir.

1282
01:28:24.299 --> 01:28:25.299
[Castle] Cash.

1283
01:28:27.136 --> 01:28:29.280
-Good to see you. partner.
-[Cash] Good to see you. too.

1284
01:28:29.304 --> 01:28:30.304
[Castle] Yeah.

1285
01:28:32.599 --> 01:28:34.351
I saw your nurse. sir.

1286
01:28:36.520 --> 01:28:38.022
I didn't fare as well.

1287
01:28:38.105 --> 01:28:39.690
Yeah.

1288
01:28:39.773 --> 01:28:42.568
I guess rank has its privileges.

1289
01:28:42.651 --> 01:28:45.529
Yeah. I guess it does. [chuckles]

1290
01:28:47.656 --> 01:28:49.199
[Cash sighs]

1291
01:28:53.328 --> 01:28:55.164
I heard the men died well. sir.

1292
01:28:58.208 --> 01:28:59.208
Yeah.

1293
01:29:00.294 --> 01:29:01.670
Yeah. that they did.

1294
01:29:02.421 --> 01:29:03.505
You survived.

1295
01:29:09.386 --> 01:29:11.388
I guess we can be grateful for that.

1296
01:29:13.599 --> 01:29:16.685
Not sure survival's all
it's cracked up to be. Cash.

1297
01:29:24.735 --> 01:29:26.820
They're sending me home. like you said.

1298
01:29:28.322 --> 01:29:30.991
Going to a hospital in Paris
and on that steamer.

1299
01:29:32.868 --> 01:29:33.868
What about you?

1300
01:29:34.870 --> 01:29:37.630
Do you finally get to go home
to that beautiful wife and boy of yours?

1301
01:29:38.123 --> 01:29:39.124
Yeah.

1302
01:29:44.797 --> 01:29:47.007
[Cash] They're saying
there may be a lot more snow.

1303
01:29:48.592 --> 01:29:51.220
Yeah. it sure isn't gonna
make this fight any easier.

1304
01:29:54.389 --> 01:29:55.808
Both sides. though. right?

1305
01:30:03.774 --> 01:30:04.774
I'll see you later. sir.

1306
01:30:05.776 --> 01:30:07.903
-Here.
-No. keep it.

1307
01:30:37.349 --> 01:30:39.852
He really said Naval-Army game?

1308
01:30:41.395 --> 01:30:42.271
He did.

1309
01:30:42.354 --> 01:30:44.857
Everybody in America knows
it's the Army-Navy game.

1310
01:30:46.817 --> 01:30:49.027
Americans fighting for the Nazis.

1311
01:30:51.321 --> 01:30:53.699
Dear Jesus. I had never
heard of that before.

1312
01:30:54.741 --> 01:30:58.912
Yeah. there were rumblings
about turncoats and spies.

1313
01:30:58.996 --> 01:31:00.038
[Mrs. Caldwell] Yeah.

1314
01:31:00.122 --> 01:31:03.542
But I was kind of like.
you know. how unlucky

1315
01:31:03.625 --> 01:31:06.461
do you really have to be
to run into one of them?

1316
01:31:07.963 --> 01:31:08.963
Very unlucky.

1317
01:31:09.006 --> 01:31:10.424
Hmm.

1318
01:31:11.925 --> 01:31:14.303
But lucky enough to make it through.

1319
01:31:14.386 --> 01:31:15.804
Well. there was definitely luck.

1320
01:31:18.640 --> 01:31:20.309
But without Lassie...

1321
01:31:21.143 --> 01:31:22.352
Oh. you think I built...

1322
01:31:23.729 --> 01:31:24.729
[Mrs. Caldwell scoffs]

1323
01:31:25.564 --> 01:31:27.316
No. [chuckles]

1324
01:31:27.399 --> 01:31:29.109
No. no. no. no. no. no.

1325
01:31:30.485 --> 01:31:31.361
No.

1326
01:31:31.445 --> 01:31:34.531
I've worked on
the assembly chain at Galvin.

1327
01:31:34.615 --> 01:31:35.866
and I did build the 300s.

1328
01:31:35.949 --> 01:31:39.411
but there's no way of knowing
for sure that I built...

1329
01:31:39.494 --> 01:31:41.580
Production unit number 5204.

1330
01:31:42.247 --> 01:31:46.001
assembly line four.
station seven. batch 52.

1331
01:31:46.752 --> 01:31:50.214
Date of issue. 11/5/1943.

1332
01:31:50.297 --> 01:31:52.466
And in charge that day.

1333
01:31:53.592 --> 01:31:54.927
Rose Caldwell.

1334
01:32:00.182 --> 01:32:01.600
You memorized it.

1335
01:32:01.683 --> 01:32:03.560
Like my children's birthdays. ma'am.

1336
01:32:06.480 --> 01:32:09.858
That might have been
the sturdiest radio in the war.

1337
01:32:09.942 --> 01:32:10.943
Hmm.

1338
01:32:12.069 --> 01:32:13.445
That was the goal.

1339
01:32:21.328 --> 01:32:22.454
Take a look at this.

1340
01:32:27.626 --> 01:32:28.752
[Mrs. Caldwell sighs]

1341
01:32:34.800 --> 01:32:35.801
Hmm.

1342
01:32:50.065 --> 01:32:51.400
Nine thousand.

1343
01:33:00.200 --> 01:33:01.618
Thank you. Colonel.

1344
01:33:05.289 --> 01:33:08.417
I have been trying to settle
with these folks for years.

1345
01:33:09.543 --> 01:33:10.877
For years.

1346
01:33:13.797 --> 01:33:15.090
Nothing doing.

1347
01:33:17.092 --> 01:33:19.261
-How did you...
-Well. I just told them

1348
01:33:19.344 --> 01:33:21.305
they should do the right thing by you.

1349
01:33:21.930 --> 01:33:23.640
an outstanding worker.

1350
01:33:24.933 --> 01:33:26.810
as a matter of principle.

1351
01:33:26.893 --> 01:33:29.229
Now that's a load of horseshit.

1352
01:33:32.691 --> 01:33:33.692
Well...

1353
01:33:36.862 --> 01:33:40.157
I may have told them
that since I'm in charge

1354
01:33:40.240 --> 01:33:44.244
of all radio equipment
purchases nationwide

1355
01:33:44.328 --> 01:33:46.038
for the United States Army that...

1356
01:33:47.456 --> 01:33:48.999
they should heed my request.

1357
01:33:49.082 --> 01:33:51.918
lest I look for another supplier.

1358
01:34:02.346 --> 01:34:03.472
[sighs]

1359
01:34:13.106 --> 01:34:14.524
Eighty years from now...

1360
01:34:17.819 --> 01:34:20.781
everyone will know the history
of what happened in that battle.

1361
01:34:22.407 --> 01:34:24.368
But will they understand it?

1362
01:34:26.745 --> 01:34:27.913
I hope they do.

1363
01:34:34.586 --> 01:34:37.047
[soft music playing]

1364
01:35:05.992 --> 01:35:09.413
Tomorrow. we'll play.
but you have to go to bed. okay?

1365
01:35:09.496 --> 01:35:10.414
[Hunter chuckles]

1366
01:35:10.497 --> 01:35:12.165
Okay. all right.

1367
01:35:12.249 --> 01:35:13.250
Who loves you. pal?

1368
01:35:13.333 --> 01:35:14.835
-[Hunter] Dad.
-That's right.

1369
01:35:17.671 --> 01:35:18.922
Go off to bed.

1370
01:35:21.758 --> 01:35:23.552
All right. this time for real now.

1371
01:35:24.594 --> 01:35:27.556
[soft music continues]

1372
01:35:35.147 --> 01:35:36.356
[light switch clicks]

1373
01:35:47.951 --> 01:35:51.455
♪ Show mercy to the hero ♪

1374
01:35:53.206 --> 01:35:57.919
♪ A pale horse haunts his fated road ♪

1375
